  <!-- 11. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE -->
  <h1>11. System Architecture</h1>
  <p>DevTrack uses a 3-Tier Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture:</p>
  <pre>
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        TIER 1: PRESENTATION LAYER                      │
│     Single Page Client (HTML5 / Vanilla CSS3 / Vanilla JavaScript)     │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ HTTP Fetch JSON (JWT Bearer Header)
┌───────────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        TIER 2: APPLICATION LAYER                       │
│     Express Server ➔ CORS & JSON Parsers ➔ JWT Auth Middleware         │
│     Express Routers ➔ Controllers (Auth, Issue, User, Dashboard)       │
└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │ Parameterized SQL Queries (mysql2)
┌───────────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        TIER 3: DATABASE LAYER                          │
│     MySQL Database Pool ➔ `users` Table ↔ `issues` Table (Foreign Keys)│
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  </pre>

  <!-- 12. APPLICATION WORKFLOW -->
  <h1>12. Application Workflow</h1>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>User Access</strong>: User opens <code>https://devtrack-system.onrender.com</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication</strong>: User registers or signs in. Backend verifies password hash via <code>bcrypt.compare()</code> and returns a signed JWT token.</li>
    <li><strong>Session Storage</strong>: Client saves JWT token to <code>localStorage</code> and renders the main dashboard.</li>
    <li><strong>Dashboard Loading</strong>: Client sends authenticated request to <code>GET /api/dashboard/stats</code>. Server calculates counts, status distribution, and priority distribution, returning JSON to update stat cards and Chart.js charts.</li>
    <li><strong>Issue Creation</strong>: User fills out Issue Modal. Client posts JSON payload to <code>POST /api/issues</code>. Controller executes SQL <code>INSERT INTO issues</code>. Server returns HTTP 201 Created. Table and charts update instantly.</li>
    <li><strong>Issue Editing / Status Change</strong>: User clicks Edit, updates status to 'Resolved', and saves. Client sends <code>PUT /api/issues/:id</code>. SQL <code>UPDATE issues</code> executes, and UI badge updates to green.</li>
    <li><strong>Issue Deletion</strong>: User clicks Delete icon, confirms prompt. Client sends <code>DELETE /api/issues/:id</code>. SQL <code>DELETE FROM issues</code> executes, and row is removed from DOM.</li>
  </ol>

