  <!-- 14. FRONTEND DOCUMENTATION -->
  <h1>14. Frontend Documentation</h1>
  <p>The frontend is built as a clean, performant Single Page Application (SPA):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>`index.html`</strong>: Contains the semantic shell, modal dialog templates, SVG icons, and panel containers (`#dashboardViewPanel`, `#issuesViewPanel`).</li>
    <li><strong>`style.css` & `dashboard.css`</strong>: Contains CSS variables for theme switching (`--bg-primary`, `--accent-primary`), flexbox/grid layouts, responsive mobile navigation drawers, status badges, and glassmorphic card effects.</li>
    <li><strong>`api.js`</strong>: Encapsulates all `fetch()` operations. Automatically injects `Authorization: Bearer <token>` into headers and handles 401 unauth session redirects.</li>
    <li><strong>`auth.js`</strong>: Handles Login and Register form submissions, token persistence in `localStorage`, and profile rendering.</li>
    <li><strong>`issues.js`</strong>: Manages table rendering, modal data population, live debounced search, multi-filters, and delete confirmations.</li>
    <li><strong>`charts.js`</strong>: Manages Chart.js doughnut and bar chart instances.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 15. BACKEND DOCUMENTATION -->
  <h1>15. Backend Documentation</h1>
  <p>The backend is built with Node.js and Express using the MVC design pattern:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>`server.js`</strong>: Initializes Express app, configures CORS, JSON parsing, static serving of `/frontend`, mounts API routes under `/api`, handles 404/500 errors, and listens on `0.0.0.0:PORT`.</li>
    <li><strong>`config/db.js`</strong>: Creates connection pool using `mysql2/promise`. Auto-creates database schema and sample data on startup. Includes clean fallback engine if external MySQL is offline.</li>
    <li><strong>`authMiddleware.js`</strong>: Verifies JWT token from incoming request headers using `JWT_SECRET`.</li>
    <li><strong>`models/issueModel.js`</strong>: Formulates parameterized SQL queries (`?`) with `LEFT JOIN` on `users` table twice to fetch reporter and assignee metadata.</li>
  </ul>

