      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/users</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Header: Bearer Token</td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, count, users }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/issues</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Query Params: search, status, priority, category, sortBy</td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, count, issues }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/issues/:id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Header: Bearer Token</td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, issue }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>POST</code></td><td><code>/api/issues</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>{ title, description, status, priority, category, assignee_id }</code></td><td>HTTP 201: <code>{ success, message, issue }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/api/issues/:id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>{ title, description, status, priority, category, assignee_id }</code></td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, message, issue }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>DELETE</code></td><td><code>/api/issues/:id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Header: Bearer Token</td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, message }</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/api/dashboard/stats</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Header: Bearer Token</td><td>HTTP 200: <code>{ success, data: { summary, statusDist, priorityDist, recent } }</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- 17. DATABASE DOCUMENTATION -->
  <h1>17. Database Documentation</h1>
  <p>The relational MySQL schema comprises two core tables defined in <code>database/schema.sql</code>:</p>

  <h3>Table 1: `users`</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Column</th>
        <th>Data Type</th>
        <th>Constraint</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>`id`</td><td>INT</td><td>PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT</td><td>Unique user identifier</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`name`</td><td>VARCHAR(100)</td><td>NOT NULL</td><td>Full user name</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`email`</td><td>VARCHAR(150)</td><td>NOT NULL, UNIQUE</td><td>User email address</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`password`</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>NOT NULL</td><td>Bcrypt salted hash</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`role`</td><td>ENUM</td><td>NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'Developer'</td><td>Developer / Tester / Project Manager / Admin</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`avatar_url`</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>DEFAULT NULL</td><td>Profile avatar image URL</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`created_at`</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</td><td>Registration timestamp</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Table 2: `issues`</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Column</th>
        <th>Data Type</th>
        <th>Constraint</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>`id`</td><td>INT</td><td>PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT</td><td>Unique issue tracking ID</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`title`</td><td>VARCHAR(255)</td><td>NOT NULL</td><td>Issue title summary</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`description`</td><td>TEXT</td><td>NULLABLE</td><td>Detailed bug description</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`status`</td><td>ENUM</td><td>NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'Open'</td><td>Open / In Progress / Resolved</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`priority`</td><td>ENUM</td><td>NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'Medium'</td><td>Low / Medium / High</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`category`</td><td>ENUM</td><td>NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'Bug'</td><td>Bug / Feature / Task / Improvement</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`reporter_id`</td><td>INT</td><td>FOREIGN KEY → users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL</td><td>User ID of bug reporter</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`assignee_id`</td><td>INT</td><td>FOREIGN KEY → users(id) ON DELETE SET NULL</td><td>User ID of assigned developer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`created_at`</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</td><td>Creation timestamp</td></tr>
      <tr><td>`updated_at`</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</td><td>Last update timestamp</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- 18. AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY -->
  <h1>18. Authentication & Security</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Password Hashing (`bcryptjs`)</strong>: Passwords are salted and hashed with 10 rounds using <code>bcrypt.hash(password, 10)</code> before SQL insertion. Plain text passwords are never stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Stateless JWT Authorization (`jsonwebtoken`)</strong>: Upon login, a JWT signed with <code>JWT_SECRET</code> is returned to the client and stored in <code>localStorage</code>. Request headers attach <code>Authorization: Bearer <token></code> for access verification.</li>
    <li><strong>SQL Injection Prevention</strong>: All queries in <code>userModel.js</code> and <code>issueModel.js</code> use parameterized statements (<code>?</code>) via <code>mysql2/promise</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Secrets Protection</strong>: Environment variables (`JWT_SECRET`, `DB_PASSWORD`) are loaded via `dotenv` and kept out of Git version control.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 19. CRUD OPERATIONS -->
  <h1>19. CRUD Operations</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Create (POST /api/issues)</strong>: Inserts new task record into `issues` table with title, description, category, status, priority, reporter ID, and assignee ID.</li>
    <li><strong>Read (GET /api/issues & GET /api/issues/:id)</strong>: Executes SQL query with `LEFT JOIN` on `users` table to fetch issue details alongside reporter and assignee names/avatars. Supports live keyword search, status filtering, and priority sorting.</li>
    <li><strong>Update (PUT /api/issues/:id)</strong>: Updates existing issue fields in database.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete (DELETE /api/issues/:id)</strong>: Executes SQL `DELETE FROM issues WHERE id = ?` to remove task records.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 20. DASHBOARD & ANALYTICS -->
  <h1>20. Dashboard & Analytics</h1>
  <p>The dashboard presents real-time aggregate statistics fetched via `GET /api/dashboard/stats`:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stat Cards</strong>: Total Issues, Open Issues, In Progress Issues, Resolved Issues, High Priority Issues.</li>
    <li><strong>Status Donut Chart</strong>: Interactive doughnut rendering breakdown of Open, In Progress, and Resolved tasks using Chart.js.</li>
    <li><strong>Priority Bar Chart</strong>: Bar chart displaying distribution of High, Medium, and Low priority issues.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 21. COMPLETE DATA FLOW -->
  <h1>21. Complete Data Flow</h1>
  <pre>
USER INPUT (Save Issue Form)
   │
   ▼
FRONTEND JS (issues.js) ➔ Formats JSON payload
   │
   ▼
API WRAPPER (api.js) ➔ Attaches 'Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>' header
   │
   ▼
EXPRESS ROUTER (issueRoutes.js) ➔ Intercepted by authMiddleware.js
   │
   ▼
CONTROLLER (issueController.createIssue) ➔ Validates required fields
   │
   ▼
MODEL (issueModel.create) ➔ Formulates SQL: INSERT INTO issues (...) VALUES (?, ?)
   │
   ▼
MYSQL DATABASE ➔ Executes query, inserts record, returns insertId
   │
   ▼
RESPONSE FLOW ➔ Controller fetches issue ➔ Returns HTTP 201 ➔ Frontend displays Toast & refreshes UI
  </pre>

  <!-- 22. UI/UX DOCUMENTATION -->
  <h1>22. UI/UX Documentation</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Auth Portal</strong>: Glassmorphic tab card allowing instant switching between Sign In and Create Account forms.</li>
    <li><strong>Navigation</strong>: Left sidebar navigation drawer with active view indicator and mobile drawer toggle button.</li>
    <li><strong>Toolbar</strong>: Filter bar containing live search input, Status filter select, Priority filter select, Category filter select, and Sort select.</li>
    <li><strong>Modals</strong>: Form modal for Creating/Editing issues, Issue Details view modal, and custom Delete confirmation dialog.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback States</strong>: Animated toast banners, empty state graphics when search returns 0 rows, loading button states.</li>
  </ul>

