  <!-- 24. ERROR HANDLING -->
  <h1>24. Error Handling</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Backend Error Handling (`errorMiddleware.js`)</strong>: Global Express middleware intercepts uncaught runtime errors, returns structured envelope `{ success: false, message: "" }`, and outputs clean server logs.</li>
    <li><strong>Database Fallback (`db.js`)</strong>: If MySQL service is unreachable, `db.js` activates the self-initializing data engine so the server starts without crashing.</li>
    <li><strong>Frontend Toast Feedback (`toast.js`)</strong>: Displays user-friendly animated green/red toast notifications for API error messages.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 25. DEPLOYMENT -->
  <h1>25. Deployment</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Platform</strong>: Render Web Service (Linux Node.js Container).</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub Repository</strong>: `https://github.com/monisha20070711-arch/devtrack-system`</li>
    <li><strong>Live URL</strong>: `https://devtrack-system.onrender.com`</li>
    <li><strong>Build & Start Commands</strong>: `npm install` and `node backend/server.js` (`npm start`).</li>
    <li><strong>Host Binding</strong>: Express server listens on host `0.0.0.0` and `process.env.PORT`.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 26. INSTALLATION & SETUP GUIDE -->
  <h1>26. Installation & Setup Guide</h1>
  <ol>
    <li>Clone repository:
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/monisha20070711-arch/devtrack-system.git
cd devtrack-system</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Install dependencies:
      <pre><code>npm install</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Configure `.env` file:
      <pre><code>PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_NAME=devtrack_db
JWT_SECRET=devtrack_secret_key</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Execute MySQL database scripts:
      <pre><code>mysql -u root -p < database/schema.sql
mysql -u root -p < database/seed.sql</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Start the server:
      <pre><code>npm start</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Open browser at <code>http://localhost:5000</code>.</li>
  </ol>

