  <!-- 34. VIVA / INTERVIEW PREPARATION (25 Q&A) -->
  <h1>34. Viva & Technical Interview Q&A (25 Questions)</h1>

  <div class="box"><strong>Q1: Why did you build DevTrack System?</strong><br>I built DevTrack to solve problem visibility in software teams by centralizing bug tracking, developer assignments, status updates, and workload metrics into a secure full-stack web dashboard.</div>

  <div class="box"><strong>Q2: What is your technology stack?</strong><br>Node.js and Express.js for the REST API backend, Vanilla HTML5/CSS3/JavaScript for the SPA frontend, MySQL for relational database storage, bcrypt and JWT for authentication, Chart.js for analytics, and Render for cloud deployment.</div>

  <div class="box"><strong>Q3: How does authentication work in DevTrack?</strong><br>Backend hashes passwords with bcrypt on registration. On login, it compares hashes and returns a signed JWT token valid for 7 days. Client stores it in localStorage and includes it in request headers as Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;.</div>

  <div class="box"><strong>Q4: How do you prevent SQL Injection?</strong><br>All queries in issueModel.js and userModel.js use parameterized statement placeholders (?) with mysql2/promise, ensuring user input is safely sanitized.</div>

  <div class="box"><strong>Q5: How do SQL JOIN queries improve performance?</strong><br>Using LEFT JOIN on users twice allows us to retrieve issue metadata, reporter name, and assignee name/avatar in a single database query, avoiding N+1 query problems.</div>

  <!-- 35. PROJECT SUMMARY FOR RESUME -->
  <h1>35. Project Summary for Resume</h1>
  <ul>
    <li>Developed and deployed a full-stack SaaS Issue & Task Management System using Node.js, Express, MySQL, and Vanilla JavaScript with JWT authentication and bcrypt encryption.</li>
    <li>Engineered a 3-tier MVC architecture with parameterized SQL queries, connection pooling, and double LEFT JOINs for developer team assignment tracking.</li>
    <li>Built a responsive SPA interface featuring Chart.js status/priority charts, real-time debounced keyword search, multi-criteria filters, and persistent Light/Dark themes; hosted live on Render.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- 36. 2-MINUTE INTERVIEW EXPLANATION -->
  <h1>36. 2-Minute Interview Explanation</h1>
  <p><em>"DevTrack is a production-style full-stack issue and task management system built with Node.js, Express, MySQL, and Vanilla Web technologies. In software projects, tracking bugs across informal chats or spreadsheets leads to unassigned defects and missed deadlines. DevTrack solves this by providing a centralized web dashboard where issues are created, assigned to team developers, and tracked through statuses—Open, In Progress, and Resolved.</em></p>

  <p><em>Technically, I selected Node.js and Express for the REST API and Vanilla JavaScript for the client interface to ensure fast load times without framework overhead. For security, I implemented bcrypt password hashing and JSON Web Tokens for stateless authorization. On the database side, I designed a relational MySQL schema with foreign keys linking tasks to team members, using SQL JOINs to fetch reporter and assignee details in a single query. I also integrated Chart.js for real-time analytics and deployed the live project on Render."</em></p>

